---
import data from '../data/payments.json';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const files = `${base}data/india-grocery/`;
const st = data.story;
const personas = [
  ['ops', 'Payments dashboard'],
  ['tests', 'Data tests'],
  ['recon', 'Reconciliation'],
  ['assistant', 'AI assistant'],
  ['store', 'Till and back office'],
  ['truth', 'What actually happened'],
];
---
<section id="payments" class="demo" data-payments-demo aria-labelledby="payments-title">
  <header class="demo-head">
    <h2 id="payments-title">Payments: the money</h2>
    <dl class="pair">
      <div><dt>The record says</dt><dd class="rec">Payment failed.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>What actually happened</dt><dd><span class="gap">The customer’s account was debited.</span></dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="demo-intro">Store 014’s tills through June 2026, and one Saturday evening when the store’s acquiring bank slowed down, as a data team reads it: the payments dashboard, the data tests, the reconciliation and an AI assistant. Change what the data team does with the records, or rerun June with the till and the back office working differently, and see each result scored against the answer key.</p>
  </header>

  <form class="controls split" aria-label="What changes" onsubmit="return false">
    <div class="control-group">
      <p class="group-head">The data team <span>works on June's records as they happened</span></p>
      <fieldset>
        <legend>How timed-out payments are read</legend>
        <div class="seg">
          <label><input type="radio" name="read" value="failed" checked /><span>As failures, as today</span></label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="read" value="matched" /><span>Matched to the provider’s report</span></label>
        </div>
        <p class="hint">A till that hears nothing back never learns the payment’s reference number. Matched by amount and time, each timeout gets the provider’s final status.</p>
      </fieldset>
      <fieldset>
        <legend>What the AI assistant is given</legend>
        <div class="seg">
          <label><input type="radio" name="ground" value="schema" checked /><span>The till’s schema</span></label>
          <label><input type="radio" name="ground" value="domain" /><span>The schema and a domain layer</span></label>
        </div>
        <p class="hint">The domain layer adds definitions, three rules, the provider’s UPI report, and two views built from them.</p>
      </fieldset>
    </div>
    <div class="control-group">
      <p class="group-head">The till and the back office <span>rerun June on the same customers</span></p>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>At the till</legend>
      <div class="seg">
        <label><input type="radio" name="till" value="retry" checked /><span>As today: ask for another payment</span></label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="till" value="check" /><span>Wait for the status check</span></label>
      </div>
      <p class="hint">Today the till gives up on a UPI payment after 30 seconds and the cashier takes another payment. NPCI allows the first status check 90 seconds after a payment.</p>
    </fieldset>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>In the back office</legend>
      <div class="seg">
        <label><input type="radio" name="recon" value="manual" checked /><span>As today: match by hand</span></label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="recon" value="bill_ref" /><span>Put the bill ID on every UPI request</span></label>
      </div>
      <p class="hint">Today UPI credits are matched to bills by amount and time, and a late credit is refunded when the customer complains. With the bill ID on each request, the next morning’s match finds it.</p>
    </fieldset>
    </div>
  </form>

  <div class="outcome" data-outcome aria-live="polite"></div>

  <div class="personas">
    <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Whose view">
      {personas.map(([key, label], i) => (
        <button type="button" role="tab" id={`py-tab-${key}`} data-persona={key} aria-selected={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'}
          aria-controls="py-panel" tabindex={i === 0 ? 0 : -1} class={key === 'truth' ? 'tab-truth' : undefined}>{label}</button>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div id="py-panel" class="panel" role="tabpanel" data-panel tabindex="0">
      <noscript>
        <p>This demo needs JavaScript. In short: on Saturday 20 June the store’s acquiring bank slowed down for 90 minutes. The tills gave up on {st.slowdown.upi_timeouts} UPI payments and took second payments, and {st.slowdown.charged_twice} customers were charged twice. The records are linked below.</p>
      </noscript>
    </div>
  </div>

  <details class="drawer">
    <summary>The records behind it</summary>
    <div class="drawer-bar">
      <div class="seg buttons" role="group" aria-label="Which records">
        <button type="button" data-rec="till" aria-pressed="true">Till payments, 20 June 18:00–20:30</button>
        <button type="button" data-rec="psp" aria-pressed="false">Provider’s UPI report</button>
        <button type="button" data-rec="settle" aria-pressed="false">Daily settlements</button>
      </div>
      <label class="reveal"><input type="checkbox" name="py-reveal" /> Show what the records hide</label>
    </div>
    <div data-records></div>
    <p class="downloads">
      Download June’s payment records as CSV:
      <a href={`${files}pos-payments-june.csv`} download>till payments</a>,
      <a href={`${files}psp-upi-report-june.csv`} download>provider’s UPI report</a>,
      <a href={`${files}upi-settlements-june.csv`} download>settlements</a>,
      <a href={`${files}upi-refunds-june.csv`} download>refunds</a>,
      <a href={`${files}customer-complaints-june.csv`} download>complaints</a>.
      <a href={`${base}data/#payments-records`}>What each file holds, and four exercises</a>.
      <a href={`${files}answer-key-payments.json`} download>Answer key</a> (spoilers).
    </p>
  </details>
</section>

<script>
  import { mountPaymentsDemo } from '../lib/payments-demo';
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-payments-demo]');
  if (root) mountPaymentsDemo(root);
</script>
